  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.outline_source.mcp.description` has one structural obligation. The `outline_source` tool definition must carry the description \"Inspect selectable items in a project file.\"\n\n`crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs#impl[Session<'_,%20D>/ToolSession<D>]/fn[definitions]` is the only implementation root. It builds the `outline_source` definition with exactly that description string. It then deserializes the definition into `ToolDefinition`. The same item carries the `{impl}` reference to the requirement.\n\nA text search for the description string found it only in that function and in the requirement and related requirement text. No other source defines it. This was a structural check only. I did not look for a test that asserts the description, and none is referenced for this requirement. I found no structural gap and no {fixme} is involved.",
